{
  "_about": "The token tree build_tokens.py turns into tokens.json. dji.com declares its token layer in the served v3 bundles (raw/css-vars.json): theme-invariant scales under core.* and the section-scoped semantics — :root .light-theme / :root .dark-theme re-declare --primary/--secondary/--tertiary/--bg/--light-bg/--border/--divider/--disabled/--reverse-*/--brand-primary-*/--brand-text-*/status roles — emitted under both light.* (.light-theme sections) and dark.* (.dark-theme sections) so each theme resolves its own value. Both are real paint: light sections (nav, listings, support) and dark sections (hero, product, footer) are measured on the live signed-out pages. Measured roles alias to the declared values where they match.",
